1
00:00:01,084 --> 00:00:03,337
[♪ theme song playing]

2
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:04,546
PARK MINJAE'S LIST

3
00:00:04,630 --> 00:00:05,923
START DATING...

4
00:00:36,620 --> 00:00:40,958
BETWEEN STEPS

5
00:00:41,583 --> 00:00:43,835
CHARACTERS, PLACES, ORGANIZATIONS,
AND EVENTS IN THIS DRAMA ARE FICTITIOUS

6
00:00:43,919 --> 00:00:45,546
THIS DRAMA CONTAINS SENSITIVE CONTENT

7
00:01:01,895 --> 00:01:03,021
It's salty.

8
00:01:03,105 --> 00:01:04,106
Salty?

9
00:01:04,189 --> 00:01:05,190
Yes.

10
00:01:06,900 --> 00:01:11,238
To me, it tasted kind of sweet...
It was sweet.

11
00:01:14,575 --> 00:01:17,578
[♪ theme song playing]

12
00:01:21,373 --> 00:01:23,041
[both grunting]

13
00:01:24,626 --> 00:01:26,211
Wait. Wait a second.

14
00:01:26,295 --> 00:01:28,463
Calm down and get a hold of yourself.

15
00:01:29,256 --> 00:01:30,591
Youjin.

16
00:01:32,217 --> 00:01:33,635
Wait.

17
00:01:33,719 --> 00:01:35,095
Wait...

18
00:01:51,028 --> 00:01:52,029
[Lim Youjin grunting]

19
00:01:52,112 --> 00:01:53,113
-My stomach.
-Oh?

20
00:01:53,196 --> 00:01:54,698
-Why? What's wrong?
-[Lim Youjin yelps]

21
00:01:54,781 --> 00:01:55,782
My stomach hurts.

22
00:01:55,866 --> 00:01:57,075
-Hey.
-It hurts so much.

23
00:01:57,159 --> 00:01:59,453
Why? Something happened to your stomach?

24
00:01:59,536 --> 00:02:01,538
-Let me see.
-[muttering in pain]

25
00:02:34,780 --> 00:02:37,783
[water running]

26
00:03:11,358 --> 00:03:13,360
[song fades]

27
00:03:13,902 --> 00:03:15,028
EPISODE 5

28
00:03:15,112 --> 00:03:16,363
-[Park Minjae] Are you okay?
-[sighs]

29
00:03:17,155 --> 00:03:19,157
-What are you doing?
-It's porridge.

30
00:03:19,700 --> 00:03:21,368
You have to eat something, right?

31
00:03:21,910 --> 00:03:23,286
You know how to make porridge?

32
00:03:23,370 --> 00:03:25,455
I'm just boiling some rice with water.

33
00:03:25,831 --> 00:03:26,832
Mm-hmm.

34
00:03:29,251 --> 00:03:30,585
You farted, right?

35
00:03:31,169 --> 00:03:32,170
What?

36
00:03:33,505 --> 00:03:35,590
Why would I fart? I don't fart.

37
00:03:35,674 --> 00:03:38,885
You're supposed to fart before eating.
You know, for digestion...

38
00:03:39,886 --> 00:03:41,638
-Because of the surgery?
-Yeah.

39
00:03:43,098 --> 00:03:44,224
Well...

40
00:03:47,185 --> 00:03:49,688
Wait, do you hear that?

41
00:03:50,772 --> 00:03:52,274
-Hear what?
-[phone vibrating]

42
00:03:52,357 --> 00:03:54,192
Oh. No, it's not me.

43
00:03:56,653 --> 00:03:58,530
No, I think your phone's ringing.

44
00:03:58,613 --> 00:03:59,698
Hmm?

45
00:04:00,699 --> 00:04:02,826
[Lim Youseong]
Hey, why weren't you answering your phone?

46
00:04:02,909 --> 00:04:04,077
Your mom's worried sick.

47
00:04:04,161 --> 00:04:05,245
Did she pick up?

48
00:04:05,328 --> 00:04:06,538
Yeah, she picked up.

49
00:04:06,621 --> 00:04:07,622
Goodness.

50
00:04:08,206 --> 00:04:09,958
Go out? Where would I go?

51
00:04:10,041 --> 00:04:12,210
I just had surgery,
and my stomach is killing me.

52
00:04:14,504 --> 00:04:16,548
No, I'm home.

53
00:04:17,174 --> 00:04:19,593
But I was in the bathroom,
so I didn't hear my phone.

54
00:04:19,676 --> 00:04:20,802
Why?

55
00:04:20,886 --> 00:04:22,471
What do you mean? You little brat!

56
00:04:22,554 --> 00:04:23,555
Jeez!

57
00:04:24,055 --> 00:04:25,223
Oh, no! [grunts]

58
00:04:27,017 --> 00:04:28,101
Hey, it's Mom.

59
00:04:28,685 --> 00:04:29,686
Did you have lunch?

60
00:04:30,937 --> 00:04:33,774
I made some porridge
and put it in the fridge.

61
00:04:34,691 --> 00:04:36,526
Heat it up, eat first,
then take your meds.

62
00:04:36,610 --> 00:04:38,737
And don't read. Just get some sleep.

63
00:04:38,820 --> 00:04:40,197
Okay, will do.

64
00:04:40,280 --> 00:04:43,492
I'll eat the porridge, take my medicine,
and go to bed. No reading.

65
00:04:45,577 --> 00:04:47,037
No, I won't study.

66
00:04:47,120 --> 00:04:48,205
Okay. Bye.

67
00:04:48,288 --> 00:04:49,915
-Bye.
-Wait.

68
00:04:49,998 --> 00:04:50,999
Hey, Lim Youjin.

69
00:04:51,082 --> 00:04:52,292
Be honest with me.

70
00:04:52,375 --> 00:04:54,169
-You're not home now, are you?
-[Seo Miyoung] Come on.

71
00:04:54,252 --> 00:04:56,630
What are you talking about? I'm home.

72
00:04:56,713 --> 00:04:57,714
Yeah?

73
00:04:58,256 --> 00:04:59,841
Then turn on the TV.

74
00:04:59,925 --> 00:05:00,926
No.

75
00:05:02,219 --> 00:05:03,220
[line disconnects]

76
00:05:03,303 --> 00:05:05,180
[Park Minjae] Why? What's up?

77
00:05:05,263 --> 00:05:07,516
I'm sorry.
I'll have porridge another time.

78
00:05:07,599 --> 00:05:09,184
I need to get home right now.

79
00:05:09,267 --> 00:05:10,352
What?

80
00:05:11,061 --> 00:05:12,145
What's going on?

81
00:05:12,771 --> 00:05:14,439
Well... I'm sorry.

82
00:05:14,523 --> 00:05:15,899
[♪ theme song playing]

83
00:05:15,982 --> 00:05:18,527
No, wait a second. Hey.

84
00:05:20,654 --> 00:05:22,405
[Lim Yongseok] What did you order?

85
00:05:22,489 --> 00:05:24,991
-Did you order mackerel?
-Yeah, and one kimchi jjim too.

86
00:05:25,951 --> 00:05:27,035
Hey, what's going on?

87
00:05:28,453 --> 00:05:30,163
-Dad, give me the car key.
-Huh?

88
00:05:30,247 --> 00:05:31,498
The car key.

89
00:05:32,874 --> 00:05:33,875
The car key.

90
00:05:41,258 --> 00:05:43,885
I don't mind taking you home. Really.

91
00:05:44,553 --> 00:05:46,471
It's okay. I can go by myself.

92
00:05:46,972 --> 00:05:50,058
But you're sick. How can you go
by yourself? Are you sure?

93
00:05:50,141 --> 00:05:51,768
Of course. I'm going to take a taxi.

94
00:05:53,061 --> 00:05:54,521
[groaning]

95
00:05:54,604 --> 00:05:56,022
Which way is it coming from?

96
00:06:04,364 --> 00:06:05,365
I'll call you.

97
00:06:06,032 --> 00:06:07,826
-Are you sure you'll be fine?
-Yeah.

98
00:06:10,120 --> 00:06:11,538
Okay. Bye then.

99
00:06:24,885 --> 00:06:26,469
Sir. Could you go a little faster?

100
00:06:26,553 --> 00:06:27,637
-I need to hurry.
-[driver] Okay.

101
00:07:07,552 --> 00:07:09,220
Excuse me, sir. Your car...

102
00:07:10,096 --> 00:07:11,264
[car alarm beeps]

103
00:07:47,175 --> 00:07:49,177
[music ends]

104
00:07:49,260 --> 00:07:50,261
[sighs]

105
00:07:53,890 --> 00:07:56,101
How long do I have
to keep eating porridge?

106
00:07:57,018 --> 00:07:58,228
Just a few more days.

107
00:07:58,311 --> 00:08:00,063
It's easier to digest than rice.

108
00:08:01,189 --> 00:08:02,607
Once you get your stitches out,

109
00:08:02,691 --> 00:08:04,609
ask the doctor
if you can eat regular food.

110
00:08:04,693 --> 00:08:05,694
Okay.

111
00:08:10,448 --> 00:08:11,574
[Seo Miyoung sighs]

112
00:08:11,658 --> 00:08:13,118
What is it now?

113
00:08:13,201 --> 00:08:15,537
Are you on a hunger strike?
Aren't you going to eat?

114
00:08:16,287 --> 00:08:18,623
Hey, then what was with those rings?

115
00:08:19,916 --> 00:08:21,334
I saw them, you little brat.

116
00:08:21,418 --> 00:08:23,753
I saw them hidden in your drawer.

117
00:08:24,754 --> 00:08:26,965
Hey, did you go through my room again?

118
00:08:27,048 --> 00:08:29,217
Don't you "hey" me. I'm your big brother!

119
00:08:29,300 --> 00:08:31,928
That's right, I went through your room.
So what?

120
00:08:32,011 --> 00:08:34,681
[groans] Mom, Lim Youseong
went through my room again.

121
00:08:34,764 --> 00:08:37,600
Well, I tried to stop him, but...

122
00:08:38,518 --> 00:08:41,312
You dummy,
why couldn't you just keep quiet?

123
00:08:41,396 --> 00:08:44,607
Fine. It wasn't nice of me
to go through your room. I accept that.

124
00:08:44,691 --> 00:08:46,192
But what was with those rings?

125
00:08:46,276 --> 00:08:47,652
Aren't they matching rings?

126
00:08:49,237 --> 00:08:51,281
I saw them, okay?

127
00:08:51,364 --> 00:08:53,575
Are you seriously going
to keep playing dumb?

128
00:08:54,784 --> 00:08:57,245
You've been lying
and seeing some guy behind our backs.

129
00:08:57,328 --> 00:08:58,538
You little sneak.

130
00:08:59,122 --> 00:09:00,123
Come on.

131
00:09:00,206 --> 00:09:03,084
What do you mean,
Youjin is seeing a guy behind our backs?

132
00:09:03,168 --> 00:09:05,378
You're just busy studying, right?

133
00:09:06,004 --> 00:09:08,131
Hey, knock it off and eat your food.

134
00:09:08,214 --> 00:09:10,925
Wow. I mean, I'm not the only one
who saw the rings here.

135
00:09:11,634 --> 00:09:13,386
Hey. Hey, you.

136
00:09:13,470 --> 00:09:15,555
Mom and Dad saw them too. Okay?

137
00:09:15,638 --> 00:09:18,391
I showed them a picture of the rings,
you little brat.

138
00:09:22,729 --> 00:09:26,483
Well, we just... I didn't mean to see it.

139
00:09:26,566 --> 00:09:28,276
He just shoved it in our faces.

140
00:09:28,985 --> 00:09:31,905
But we wanted to respect your privacy,

141
00:09:31,988 --> 00:09:34,532
so we didn't bring it up,
even though we were curious.

142
00:09:34,616 --> 00:09:36,451
See? Mom is curious too.

143
00:09:37,452 --> 00:09:39,412
Did those rings

144
00:09:39,996 --> 00:09:43,333
have my name or initials engraved on them?

145
00:09:46,211 --> 00:09:48,838
So... they're not your rings?

146
00:09:49,631 --> 00:09:50,632
They're not yours?

147
00:09:52,801 --> 00:09:53,802
Now,

148
00:09:54,803 --> 00:09:56,846
let me present a hypothesis

149
00:09:56,930 --> 00:09:59,140
that's mathematical,
logical, and philosophical.

150
00:09:59,224 --> 00:10:00,809
It's only a hypothesis, though.

151
00:10:01,226 --> 00:10:02,227
[Lim Youseong sighs]

152
00:10:02,310 --> 00:10:05,688
Detective Conan, one truth prevails!

153
00:10:07,774 --> 00:10:11,861
What if they were Lim Youseong's rings
to begin with, not mine?

154
00:10:12,487 --> 00:10:13,488
What?

155
00:10:14,948 --> 00:10:18,118
He'd actually had those rings
for a long time.

156
00:10:18,618 --> 00:10:20,954
He had bought them
for his girlfriend at the time,

157
00:10:21,037 --> 00:10:22,997
but she turned down his proposal.

158
00:10:24,082 --> 00:10:27,085
Then he used those same rings
to frame his younger sister.

159
00:10:27,836 --> 00:10:29,087
Are you nuts?

160
00:10:29,170 --> 00:10:32,674
Come on. Would he really go that far
just to frame you? Why?

161
00:10:33,258 --> 00:10:36,261
I know you guys fight all the time,
but that's too much...

162
00:10:37,262 --> 00:10:41,182
Because his younger sister
knows one of his secrets.

163
00:10:41,766 --> 00:10:43,768
Secret? What is it?

164
00:10:45,854 --> 00:10:49,023
The truth is,
those rings actually belonged...

165
00:10:51,192 --> 00:10:55,029
to a former employee
of Cheil Auto Repair Shop, Lee Jihye--

166
00:10:55,113 --> 00:10:56,865
-Hey! You little...
-Jeez, you scared me.

167
00:11:00,243 --> 00:11:01,619
[exhales sharply]

168
00:11:03,288 --> 00:11:04,289
You're real nasty.

169
00:11:07,083 --> 00:11:08,084
What...

170
00:11:12,672 --> 00:11:13,673
Lee Jihye?

171
00:11:14,632 --> 00:11:17,302
From last year...
No, was it two years ago?

172
00:11:18,011 --> 00:11:20,471
That girl who used to work
at our office, right?

173
00:11:20,555 --> 00:11:23,641
Yeah. So that's why she quit.

174
00:11:24,058 --> 00:11:25,059
Oh.

175
00:11:25,143 --> 00:11:26,644
How did you know about that?

176
00:11:27,228 --> 00:11:29,439
I don't. That was just a hypothesis.

177
00:11:31,524 --> 00:11:33,693
Jeez, that was mean.

178
00:11:34,194 --> 00:11:38,031
You go to Seohan National University.
Don't stoop to his level.

179
00:11:38,990 --> 00:11:39,991
Yeah.

180
00:11:41,117 --> 00:11:43,536
Have some compassion for him.

181
00:11:43,620 --> 00:11:46,331
[breath trembling]

182
00:11:46,414 --> 00:11:49,042
[quietly] I will find you at all costs.

183
00:11:49,959 --> 00:11:54,005
I will find you
and make you pay, you little...

184
00:11:57,133 --> 00:12:00,136
[breath trembling]

185
00:12:09,145 --> 00:12:11,147
[massager vibrating]

186
00:12:11,314 --> 00:12:14,317
[♪ pensive music playing]

187
00:12:16,611 --> 00:12:18,196
[sighs]

188
00:12:21,741 --> 00:12:22,742
[massager stops]

189
00:12:29,082 --> 00:12:30,083
[grunts]

190
00:12:52,814 --> 00:12:55,817
[Kim Sejin muttering]
X and Y already knew each other.

191
00:12:56,317 --> 00:12:59,988
X was in fashion and textiles,
and Y is in mechanical engineering.

192
00:13:02,573 --> 00:13:05,076
How did they know each other
from different departments?

193
00:13:05,910 --> 00:13:07,120
X...

194
00:13:07,787 --> 00:13:11,708
had also gone on blind dates
with C, D, and E,

195
00:13:12,834 --> 00:13:14,043
all arranged by Y.

196
00:13:14,127 --> 00:13:15,128
Why?

197
00:13:16,296 --> 00:13:18,423
[sighing heavily]

198
00:13:19,382 --> 00:13:22,677
[inhales]
X had tried to meet Y in private.

199
00:13:22,760 --> 00:13:24,178
Even went to Y's house.

200
00:13:24,721 --> 00:13:25,722
Why?

201
00:13:29,225 --> 00:13:30,601
Is X a man-eater?

202
00:13:31,644 --> 00:13:32,812
A queen bee?

203
00:13:32,895 --> 00:13:33,896
Beekeeping?

204
00:13:34,647 --> 00:13:36,399
Y is kind of clueless.

205
00:13:37,984 --> 00:13:41,487
Into married women?

206
00:13:43,865 --> 00:13:46,617
But what would those two
have to talk about in private?

207
00:13:48,870 --> 00:13:50,079
Some kind of secret?

208
00:13:52,457 --> 00:13:55,752
References. I need references.

209
00:14:12,351 --> 00:14:13,352
[sighs]

210
00:14:23,946 --> 00:14:24,947
[indistinct chatter]

211
00:14:30,328 --> 00:14:32,080
-[sighs]
-[soft tinkling]

212
00:14:42,632 --> 00:14:43,800
[door opens]

213
00:14:44,592 --> 00:14:46,219
Hey, good morning.

214
00:14:46,803 --> 00:14:47,970
[Kim Sejin] Hello.

215
00:14:52,934 --> 00:14:55,353
So Lim Youjin is coming back
to the lab starting today?

216
00:14:55,436 --> 00:14:56,437
Huh?

217
00:14:57,146 --> 00:14:58,439
Yeah, she is.

218
00:14:59,482 --> 00:15:00,900
[Kim Sejin] But she hasn't shown up yet.

219
00:15:05,655 --> 00:15:07,365
It's not time yet.

220
00:15:07,448 --> 00:15:08,449
Nobody's here.

221
00:15:20,169 --> 00:15:22,797
So, what was...

222
00:15:24,757 --> 00:15:27,093
Lim Youjin doing at your place that day?

223
00:15:29,262 --> 00:15:30,638
That day?

224
00:15:30,721 --> 00:15:33,057
She had a question
about something in a paper.

225
00:15:33,641 --> 00:15:37,395
Well, then she could've
just emailed or called you.

226
00:15:38,813 --> 00:15:41,232
I know. So I told her
to just email me next time.

227
00:15:43,151 --> 00:15:44,152
[sighing]

228
00:15:46,529 --> 00:15:47,572
What?

229
00:15:49,866 --> 00:15:51,033
-Nothing.
-[door opens]

230
00:15:51,117 --> 00:15:52,451
Hello.

231
00:15:52,535 --> 00:15:53,953
-[Kim Sejin] Hello.
-Hi.

232
00:15:56,581 --> 00:15:58,207
Good morning.

233
00:15:58,291 --> 00:15:59,417
Hello.

234
00:15:59,500 --> 00:16:00,668
[door closes]

235
00:16:16,392 --> 00:16:17,476
[honking]

236
00:16:31,741 --> 00:16:34,368
Call me when you're done.
I'll come pick you up.

237
00:16:36,329 --> 00:16:37,747
I can get home by myself.

238
00:16:38,539 --> 00:16:41,500
You don't have to drive me anymore.
My stitches are out. I'm fine.

239
00:16:41,584 --> 00:16:43,211
Mom is worried.

240
00:16:44,212 --> 00:16:45,713
Let me drive you a few more days.

241
00:16:49,508 --> 00:16:50,509
[both sighing]

242
00:16:50,593 --> 00:16:52,595
Look, you started it, okay?

243
00:16:53,429 --> 00:16:55,640
Why did you have to go through my room?

244
00:16:56,265 --> 00:16:58,059
Dude, you crossed the line first.

245
00:16:58,142 --> 00:17:00,144
"Dude"? Did you just call me "dude"?

246
00:17:01,103 --> 00:17:02,980
Hey, you know what?

247
00:17:03,064 --> 00:17:05,399
You've always disrespected me like that.

248
00:17:05,900 --> 00:17:09,528
And I've always let it slide
because you're my only sister.

249
00:17:09,612 --> 00:17:11,113
I told myself, "Fine, it's cute."

250
00:17:11,197 --> 00:17:13,824
"Go ahead and walk all over me.
Do whatever you want."

251
00:17:13,908 --> 00:17:15,576
But this time, you crossed the line.

252
00:17:16,619 --> 00:17:17,620
Sorry.

253
00:17:17,703 --> 00:17:20,331
Save it. Don't bother apologizing.
I won't accept it.

254
00:17:20,414 --> 00:17:21,749
From now on, we're at war.

255
00:17:23,084 --> 00:17:25,670
I'll find your boyfriend
no matter what it takes,

256
00:17:25,753 --> 00:17:28,464
and I'm going to expose you
for the snake you really are.

257
00:17:28,547 --> 00:17:29,549
Now get lost.

258
00:17:29,632 --> 00:17:31,801
-Get out! Go.
-[scoffs]

259
00:17:38,558 --> 00:17:39,559
Youjin.

260
00:17:41,102 --> 00:17:42,520
One truth prevails.

261
00:17:43,437 --> 00:17:44,438
Freak.

262
00:17:44,522 --> 00:17:46,524
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

263
00:18:04,041 --> 00:18:05,251
[tires screeching]

264
00:18:08,713 --> 00:18:10,715
[♪ music increases in tempo]

265
00:18:21,726 --> 00:18:22,727
Youseong.

266
00:18:23,728 --> 00:18:24,895
Subin. Hey.

267
00:18:26,230 --> 00:18:27,356
What are you doing here?

268
00:18:29,025 --> 00:18:30,860
-How about we sit here?
-Yeah, sure.

269
00:18:37,408 --> 00:18:40,286
How come you don't come over anymore?
Are you that busy?

270
00:18:40,411 --> 00:18:43,414
Uh, yeah, pretty busy.

271
00:18:43,497 --> 00:18:46,500
I need to study and have lab work to do.

272
00:18:46,584 --> 00:18:47,710
That's why.

273
00:18:47,793 --> 00:18:50,129
But what brings you to our campus?

274
00:18:50,212 --> 00:18:54,258
Youjin had her appendix taken out,
so I'm giving her rides for a few days.

275
00:18:54,842 --> 00:18:57,094
Right, I heard about her surgery.
I meant to visit.

276
00:18:57,178 --> 00:18:58,554
She's already back at the lab?

277
00:18:58,638 --> 00:19:01,307
Getting your appendix out
is hardly even surgery, you know.

278
00:19:01,390 --> 00:19:03,684
She got out quickly,
and she's been eating fine.

279
00:19:03,768 --> 00:19:05,686
Really? That's great to hear.

280
00:19:06,687 --> 00:19:09,065
A little later,
and it would have been bad.

281
00:19:09,148 --> 00:19:12,234
But someone got her to the hospital
before her appendix burst,

282
00:19:12,860 --> 00:19:16,322
so they got to operate on time,
and she's recovering pretty fast.

283
00:19:16,405 --> 00:19:17,615
That's a relief.

284
00:19:18,616 --> 00:19:23,621
And I heard the person who took her
to the hospital was a professor here.

285
00:19:23,704 --> 00:19:24,830
Do you know who it is?

286
00:19:24,914 --> 00:19:25,915
What?

287
00:19:26,415 --> 00:19:27,541
A professor?

288
00:19:27,625 --> 00:19:29,960
I hear he's tall and handsome.

289
00:19:30,461 --> 00:19:33,297
He's a professor in his early to mid-30s.

290
00:19:33,964 --> 00:19:36,175
I mean, are there professors that young?

291
00:19:37,051 --> 00:19:38,177
I'm not sure.

292
00:19:39,053 --> 00:19:40,513
Isn't he one of your professors?

293
00:19:41,097 --> 00:19:43,808
No, we don't have any professors
like that in our department.

294
00:19:43,891 --> 00:19:44,934
Oh!

295
00:19:45,017 --> 00:19:47,019
Maybe he's a mechanical
engineering professor?

296
00:19:47,103 --> 00:19:49,188
There's a professor like that there?

297
00:19:50,231 --> 00:19:53,859
I actually don't know much
about that department.

298
00:19:53,943 --> 00:19:55,236
You should ask Youjin.

299
00:19:55,319 --> 00:19:57,154
She won't tell me, so...

300
00:19:57,780 --> 00:19:58,781
Why not?

301
00:19:59,740 --> 00:20:00,741
Hmm...

302
00:20:01,701 --> 00:20:03,994
Oh! Could it be him?

303
00:20:04,078 --> 00:20:05,246
Who?

304
00:20:05,329 --> 00:20:08,082
There's this tall and handsome...

305
00:20:08,749 --> 00:20:11,252
But he's not a professor.
He's just an assistant.

306
00:20:11,836 --> 00:20:14,547
He's an assistant, not a professor?

307
00:20:14,630 --> 00:20:15,923
Ah.

308
00:20:16,882 --> 00:20:18,384
What's his name?

309
00:20:18,968 --> 00:20:19,969
Oh.

310
00:20:21,178 --> 00:20:22,346
Hmm...

311
00:20:23,013 --> 00:20:26,016
I think you should ask Youjin.

312
00:20:29,687 --> 00:20:30,813
Subin.

313
00:20:32,398 --> 00:20:33,649
Look at this.

314
00:20:37,153 --> 00:20:39,905
He's Youjin's boyfriend.

315
00:20:41,407 --> 00:20:42,408
Really?

316
00:20:42,491 --> 00:20:43,743
Yeah.

317
00:20:43,826 --> 00:20:45,453
That's why she wouldn't tell us.

318
00:20:45,536 --> 00:20:48,372
We wanted to thank him,
but she said there was no need.

319
00:20:50,875 --> 00:20:53,252
Then I don't think it's him.

320
00:20:53,335 --> 00:20:54,462
What?

321
00:20:55,045 --> 00:20:57,965
That assistant guy has a disability.

322
00:20:58,466 --> 00:21:02,428
If he were her boyfriend, she wouldn't
have offered to set me up with him.

323
00:21:02,511 --> 00:21:03,512
That wouldn't make sense.

324
00:21:04,722 --> 00:21:05,931
He's disabled?

325
00:21:08,517 --> 00:21:11,103
Uh... I mean...

326
00:21:12,021 --> 00:21:17,026
Youjin offered to set me up with him,
saying he's a really nice guy.

327
00:21:17,109 --> 00:21:19,737
But how could she set you up
with someone like that?

328
00:21:19,820 --> 00:21:20,821
That's messed up.

329
00:21:20,905 --> 00:21:22,072
No, it's not like that.

330
00:21:22,156 --> 00:21:25,659
-She said he's a really nice guy.
-[chuckles softly]

331
00:21:25,743 --> 00:21:28,162
Of course. I feel bad now.

332
00:21:32,291 --> 00:21:34,460
So, what's his name?

333
00:21:35,795 --> 00:21:37,797
[♪ whimsical music playing]

334
00:21:55,773 --> 00:21:57,983
Should we start the meeting now?

335
00:22:01,028 --> 00:22:03,614
Chansoo, I can't see the board
very well from there.

336
00:22:03,697 --> 00:22:04,698
Can I sit here?

337
00:22:04,782 --> 00:22:06,283
-Okay, sure.
-Thank you.

338
00:22:11,247 --> 00:22:12,373
[Choi Hangyeol grunts]

339
00:22:17,670 --> 00:22:21,131
[♪ whimsical music continues]

340
00:22:30,391 --> 00:22:31,892
Youjin, how are you feeling?

341
00:22:32,476 --> 00:22:34,562
I got my stitches out. I'm fine.

342
00:22:34,645 --> 00:22:35,646
That's great.

343
00:22:35,729 --> 00:22:37,731
Still, you didn't have
to come back so soon.

344
00:22:37,815 --> 00:22:39,817
You could've taken some more time off.

345
00:22:40,568 --> 00:22:42,152
I love coming to school.

346
00:22:42,236 --> 00:22:44,154
I always look forward to seeing you guys.

347
00:22:44,989 --> 00:22:46,282
But still.

348
00:22:46,365 --> 00:22:47,992
Don't push yourself too hard, okay?

349
00:22:48,075 --> 00:22:49,618
Work can wait.

350
00:22:49,702 --> 00:22:51,871
[Park Minjae]
Yeah, you need to take care of yourself.

351
00:22:51,954 --> 00:22:53,289
You're an adult.

352
00:22:53,372 --> 00:22:54,373
Okay, will do.

353
00:22:59,587 --> 00:23:02,339
Did you bring the modeling illustrations
you said you'd do?

354
00:23:03,716 --> 00:23:06,051
No, I haven't finished yet.

355
00:23:06,135 --> 00:23:07,136
Sorry.

356
00:23:07,219 --> 00:23:10,180
Hey, you said you'd do it.

357
00:23:11,265 --> 00:23:12,600
[Bae Chansoo]
She was sick and had surgery.

358
00:23:12,683 --> 00:23:14,268
How could she have gotten it done?

359
00:23:14,768 --> 00:23:16,687
If she agreed to it,
she should've done it.

360
00:23:16,770 --> 00:23:18,314
If not, she should've told us.

361
00:23:18,397 --> 00:23:23,360
Why don't you just let her handle it
and focus on your own work, Sejin?

362
00:23:23,444 --> 00:23:25,738
I'm doing my own work just fine.

363
00:23:26,405 --> 00:23:27,656
Are you talking back to me?

364
00:23:27,740 --> 00:23:29,575
I'm not talking back to you. I'm saying...

365
00:23:29,658 --> 00:23:31,243
[Park Minjae] Hey. That's enough, okay?

366
00:23:31,327 --> 00:23:34,204
It's not a big deal.
Are you really fighting over this?

367
00:23:34,872 --> 00:23:36,665
You've gotten a little too comfortable.

368
00:23:37,750 --> 00:23:39,835
It's been a while.
Want to go back to Dieland?

369
00:23:39,919 --> 00:23:41,253
Should I give Seohyun a call?

370
00:23:41,337 --> 00:23:42,588
INCOMING CALL
CHACHA

371
00:23:43,255 --> 00:23:44,590
[cell phone vibrating]

372
00:23:45,090 --> 00:23:46,842
The professor was already asking

373
00:23:46,926 --> 00:23:49,929
when the upper-body finite element
analysis results would be ready.

374
00:23:50,429 --> 00:23:52,306
He wanted the results by this afternoon,

375
00:23:52,890 --> 00:23:56,226
but we haven't even finished
the modeling yet.

376
00:23:57,561 --> 00:23:58,687
[cell phone vibrating]

377
00:23:59,813 --> 00:24:02,232
INCOMING CALL
CHACHA

378
00:24:02,316 --> 00:24:04,151
[muttering] Why does she keep calling me?

379
00:24:04,234 --> 00:24:06,904
So stop sitting around bickering

380
00:24:06,987 --> 00:24:09,239
-and start generating some data.
-[cellphone vibrating]

381
00:24:09,323 --> 00:24:10,866
You're not undergrads anymore.

382
00:24:10,950 --> 00:24:13,160
Do I really have to nag you
over basic stuff?

383
00:24:13,243 --> 00:24:14,244
[softly] Hello.

384
00:24:14,328 --> 00:24:15,996
What are you doing in a meeting?

385
00:24:16,997 --> 00:24:18,832
Chacha wants to talk to you.

386
00:24:18,916 --> 00:24:20,250
Why did you take that...

387
00:24:20,334 --> 00:24:21,335
Hello?

388
00:24:22,378 --> 00:24:23,379
[sighs]

389
00:24:23,462 --> 00:24:24,922
Huh?

390
00:24:25,005 --> 00:24:26,131
What?

391
00:24:26,215 --> 00:24:27,675
Friday? What about Friday?

392
00:24:27,758 --> 00:24:30,094
You're supposed to go
to the musical that day.

393
00:24:30,177 --> 00:24:33,055
Those tickets were really hard to get.
So don't be late.

394
00:24:33,138 --> 00:24:35,349
Look up some good restaurants nearby too.

395
00:24:36,183 --> 00:24:38,644
Actually, never mind. I'll do that too.

396
00:24:38,727 --> 00:24:40,396
You're clueless about trendy places.

397
00:24:40,479 --> 00:24:42,064
I don't care about trendy...

398
00:24:42,147 --> 00:24:43,774
I'm busy. I'm in a meeting. Bye.

399
00:24:44,733 --> 00:24:45,734
[line disconnects]

400
00:24:46,610 --> 00:24:48,529
Minjae, is that about the blind date?

401
00:24:48,612 --> 00:24:49,613
Right?

402
00:24:50,322 --> 00:24:51,740
You should go for it.

403
00:24:51,824 --> 00:24:55,494
She looked pretty in that picture,
and you two looked good together.

404
00:24:56,996 --> 00:24:58,622
That's not true.

405
00:24:58,706 --> 00:25:00,916
Anyway, enough about that. Where were we?

406
00:25:01,750 --> 00:25:03,836
-Huh?
-We hadn't really gotten anywhere yet.

407
00:25:04,753 --> 00:25:05,838
No, wait.

408
00:25:06,338 --> 00:25:09,091
Yeah. How far have we gotten
with the modeling illustrations?

409
00:25:09,174 --> 00:25:10,759
Lim Youjin didn't do it.

410
00:25:11,552 --> 00:25:12,553
Youjin...

411
00:25:16,265 --> 00:25:17,850
[sighs softly]

412
00:25:35,159 --> 00:25:36,577
[cellphone vibrating]

413
00:25:38,203 --> 00:25:39,204
Yeah.

414
00:25:40,039 --> 00:25:42,124
I just stepped out. I'm on a coffee run.

415
00:25:43,584 --> 00:25:45,919
I have to feed them
to get their brains going.

416
00:25:48,172 --> 00:25:49,173
What?

417
00:25:49,882 --> 00:25:50,883
Why?

418
00:25:52,301 --> 00:25:55,095
Come on, you have to go on three dates
before you can tell.

419
00:25:56,346 --> 00:25:57,347
[yells] Hey!

420
00:26:01,226 --> 00:26:04,104
[softly] You think you're the only one
who's busy? We're all busy.

421
00:26:05,105 --> 00:26:08,025
Park Minjae,
you're not seeing someone, are you?

422
00:26:08,609 --> 00:26:11,028
What are you talking about?
I'm not seeing anyone.

423
00:26:11,862 --> 00:26:12,946
Well,

424
00:26:14,031 --> 00:26:16,867
it's not like I'm anything special

425
00:26:17,576 --> 00:26:19,787
or have much more to offer
than other people.

426
00:26:21,288 --> 00:26:22,331
And honestly...

427
00:26:23,415 --> 00:26:27,002
uh... I don't even know if I'm qualified.

428
00:26:27,586 --> 00:26:29,630
Qualified? Qualified for what?

429
00:26:31,090 --> 00:26:33,092
You say the weirdest things sometimes.

430
00:26:34,009 --> 00:26:35,010
I mean, sure,

431
00:26:35,803 --> 00:26:38,055
your personality
isn't exactly your strong suit.

432
00:26:38,138 --> 00:26:40,557
You overthink everything,
and you're stubborn.

433
00:26:42,184 --> 00:26:44,436
But who dates for personality these days?

434
00:26:44,520 --> 00:26:45,604
It's all about looks.

435
00:26:47,481 --> 00:26:49,608
And you're pretty good-looking.

436
00:26:50,317 --> 00:26:51,318
Yeah?

437
00:26:52,194 --> 00:26:53,195
I am?

438
00:26:53,862 --> 00:26:54,863
[knock at door]

439
00:26:54,947 --> 00:26:56,490
Someone's here. I have to go.

440
00:26:56,573 --> 00:26:57,574
Bye.

441
00:26:58,242 --> 00:26:59,243
[line disconnects]

442
00:26:59,326 --> 00:27:01,203
-Yes?
-[door opens]

443
00:27:04,039 --> 00:27:05,082
How can I help you?

444
00:27:05,582 --> 00:27:10,337
Uh, hi. Do you know someone
named Lim Youjin in this lab?

445
00:27:11,839 --> 00:27:12,840
Who are you?

446
00:27:13,841 --> 00:27:16,260
Hello, my name is Lim Youseong.

447
00:27:16,343 --> 00:27:17,845
I'm Youjin's older brother.

448
00:27:17,928 --> 00:27:18,929
[dramatic sting]

449
00:27:19,012 --> 00:27:20,764
[hesitating] I see. Okay.

450
00:27:23,016 --> 00:27:24,309
[Choi Hangyeol]
Let's move it forward first.

451
00:27:24,393 --> 00:27:25,394
-[Eom Taeho] Okay.
-[Choi Hangyeol] Move forward.

452
00:27:25,477 --> 00:27:27,855
[♪ upbeat music playing]

453
00:27:30,232 --> 00:27:31,316
Hangyeol.

454
00:27:33,026 --> 00:27:34,111
Try moving it backward.

455
00:27:34,194 --> 00:27:35,696
Backward? Okay, moving backward.

456
00:27:41,994 --> 00:27:43,036
-[cellphone vibrating]
-Oh?

457
00:27:43,120 --> 00:27:44,830
Sorry, excuse me for a moment.

458
00:27:46,456 --> 00:27:47,958
Subin, I'll call you back.

459
00:27:50,377 --> 00:27:51,378
What?

460
00:27:51,461 --> 00:27:52,880
My brother?

461
00:27:54,006 --> 00:27:55,007
When?

462
00:27:55,632 --> 00:27:56,633
Yeah.

463
00:27:57,259 --> 00:27:58,260
Yeah.

464
00:27:59,970 --> 00:28:00,971
What?

465
00:28:01,763 --> 00:28:04,182
What a nut.
Seriously, has he lost his mind?

466
00:28:05,267 --> 00:28:07,019
Okay, just hang up for now.

467
00:28:08,812 --> 00:28:12,065
I'm so sorry, but something came up.
I need to step out for a minute.

468
00:28:12,149 --> 00:28:13,859
-Hey!
-I promise. Just a sec.

469
00:28:13,942 --> 00:28:14,943
Hey!

470
00:28:15,611 --> 00:28:16,820
[Kang Miran] What's wrong?

471
00:28:19,406 --> 00:28:21,658
Maybe I shouldn't have
told her brother about it.

472
00:28:22,159 --> 00:28:25,913
What brother would be happy to hear
that his sister's boyfriend is disabled?

473
00:28:25,996 --> 00:28:26,997
They'd be shocked.

474
00:28:27,998 --> 00:28:29,583
He's not her boyfriend.

475
00:28:30,500 --> 00:28:31,668
He's not.

476
00:28:32,252 --> 00:28:34,338
Then things should get cleared up soon.

477
00:28:40,636 --> 00:28:41,803
Wait.

478
00:28:42,304 --> 00:28:44,806
Could that research assistant
be into Youjin?

479
00:29:07,579 --> 00:29:10,457
This is all I have to offer right now.

480
00:29:10,540 --> 00:29:11,541
I'm sorry.

481
00:29:11,667 --> 00:29:14,086
No. This is great.

482
00:29:14,169 --> 00:29:15,170
Okay.

483
00:29:18,006 --> 00:29:19,091
So...

484
00:29:19,925 --> 00:29:24,012
Should I try giving Ms. Lim Youjin a call?

485
00:29:24,096 --> 00:29:25,681
No. Forget about Youjin.

486
00:29:26,348 --> 00:29:30,352
To tell you the truth,
I'm here to see you, Mr. Park Minjae.

487
00:29:31,144 --> 00:29:32,229
Me?

488
00:29:33,105 --> 00:29:34,856
But sir, why would you...

489
00:29:34,940 --> 00:29:36,566
Don't call me sir.

490
00:29:36,650 --> 00:29:38,151
I'm just Youjin's brother.

491
00:29:38,944 --> 00:29:41,071
Right, her brother. Right.

492
00:29:41,154 --> 00:29:44,116
So, as her brother,
why did you want to see me?

493
00:29:44,199 --> 00:29:46,785
It's nothing much.

494
00:29:46,868 --> 00:29:50,163
I've basically left her here
without ever properly introducing myself,

495
00:29:50,247 --> 00:29:52,874
-so figured I'd stop by while I was here.
-Ah!

496
00:29:53,000 --> 00:29:55,752
Thank you for always looking out for her.
I owe you so much.

497
00:29:55,836 --> 00:29:57,170
Not at all.

498
00:29:57,254 --> 00:30:00,841
Ms. Lim Youjin is really kind
and hardworking.

499
00:30:00,924 --> 00:30:03,969
She's absolutely indispensable to our lab.

500
00:30:04,052 --> 00:30:06,054
A truly exceptional researcher, yes.

501
00:30:06,596 --> 00:30:08,598
The professors
speak very highly of her too.

502
00:30:08,682 --> 00:30:10,434
-Really?
-Yes.

503
00:30:10,517 --> 00:30:12,853
I'm glad to hear
that they think so highly of her.

504
00:30:19,401 --> 00:30:21,361
Should I give Youjin a call?

505
00:30:21,445 --> 00:30:23,739
No. I actually came here because...

506
00:30:23,822 --> 00:30:24,823
Yes?

507
00:30:25,741 --> 00:30:28,160
There's something I wanted to ask you.

508
00:30:28,243 --> 00:30:30,370
Sure, what is it?

509
00:30:30,454 --> 00:30:32,748
When Youjin had appendicitis
the other day...

510
00:30:32,831 --> 00:30:34,124
Yes.

511
00:30:34,207 --> 00:30:37,961
I heard a male professor here
took her to the hospital.

512
00:30:38,045 --> 00:30:40,047
I was wondering
if you might know who it was.

513
00:30:41,673 --> 00:30:42,674
A professor?

514
00:30:42,758 --> 00:30:45,594
Yes. I hear he's really tall and handsome.

515
00:30:45,677 --> 00:30:48,513
He's a male professor
in his early to mid-30s.

516
00:30:49,473 --> 00:30:51,475
Is there a professor that young?

517
00:30:51,558 --> 00:30:54,519
[muttering]

518
00:30:54,603 --> 00:30:56,438
Well, I'm not sure.

519
00:30:57,230 --> 00:31:01,109
I'd really like to meet him
and say thank you.

520
00:31:01,193 --> 00:31:02,402
Oh.

521
00:31:02,486 --> 00:31:03,695
Do you know who he is?

522
00:31:03,779 --> 00:31:06,698
No, I've never heard about this.

523
00:31:07,532 --> 00:31:08,658
Uh...

524
00:31:09,201 --> 00:31:11,620
Why don't you ask Youjin yourself?

525
00:31:11,703 --> 00:31:13,705
I did, but she wouldn't tell me.

526
00:31:13,789 --> 00:31:15,373
She's keeping it to herself.

527
00:31:16,666 --> 00:31:17,667
Why?

528
00:31:17,751 --> 00:31:20,003
I don't know why she'd keep it to herself.

529
00:31:22,380 --> 00:31:23,799
You really don't know?

530
00:31:23,882 --> 00:31:26,468
No, this is the first time
I've heard about it.

531
00:31:29,763 --> 00:31:30,972
Then...

532
00:31:34,476 --> 00:31:36,228
Have you seen something like this?

533
00:31:36,937 --> 00:31:39,397
What... is this?

534
00:31:40,482 --> 00:31:42,067
Youseong, It's not him.

535
00:31:42,192 --> 00:31:44,444
It's... It's someone else.
There's someone else.

536
00:31:44,945 --> 00:31:47,697
I'll take you to meet him. Come on out.

537
00:31:47,781 --> 00:31:49,783
I'm just having some coffee. What's up?

538
00:31:49,866 --> 00:31:52,786
You win, okay? I'm sorry.
Now, hurry up and come on out.

539
00:31:52,869 --> 00:31:53,954
What... Hey.

540
00:31:54,037 --> 00:31:56,331
Hey, wait.
I need to say goodbye, you know.

541
00:31:56,414 --> 00:31:57,499
I'll see you next time.

542
00:31:57,582 --> 00:31:59,292
-Okay. Take care.
-Come on.

543
00:31:59,376 --> 00:32:01,086
What kind of research do you do here?

544
00:32:07,592 --> 00:32:08,760
[Lim Youseong] Hey, let go of me.

545
00:32:08,844 --> 00:32:10,637
-Let go of me!
-Could you just...

546
00:32:10,720 --> 00:32:12,180
You're hurting my arm, you brat.

547
00:32:12,264 --> 00:32:13,431
-Let go.
-Gosh.

548
00:32:14,850 --> 00:32:15,851
Seriously.

549
00:32:16,518 --> 00:32:18,145
So why did you cross the line?

550
00:32:18,687 --> 00:32:20,647
You crossed the line first, you know?

551
00:32:21,273 --> 00:32:23,275
You're the one who started this. Okay?

552
00:32:28,155 --> 00:32:29,156
[sighs]

553
00:32:33,869 --> 00:32:36,371
[Lim Youseong] I should've stopped by
to introduce myself sooner.

554
00:32:37,289 --> 00:32:39,958
Nice to meet you.
I'm Lim Youseong, Youjin's older brother.

555
00:32:40,542 --> 00:32:41,543
I'm Lee Jihoon.

556
00:32:41,626 --> 00:32:42,627
Oh.

557
00:32:42,711 --> 00:32:46,631
I heard things could've gone really bad
if it hadn't been for you.

558
00:32:47,924 --> 00:32:48,925
Thank you so much.

559
00:32:49,009 --> 00:32:50,302
You saved her life.

560
00:32:50,385 --> 00:32:51,386
Not at all.

561
00:32:51,469 --> 00:32:54,097
I just happened to come across her
and took her to the hospital.

562
00:32:54,806 --> 00:32:57,934
By the way, you're really young
for a math professor.

563
00:32:58,852 --> 00:32:59,853
Wow.

564
00:32:59,936 --> 00:33:01,062
Are you married, by any chance?

565
00:33:01,730 --> 00:33:03,231
Uh, no, not yet.

566
00:33:03,315 --> 00:33:04,858
I see. You're not.

567
00:33:05,525 --> 00:33:07,027
What about a girlfriend?

568
00:33:07,110 --> 00:33:09,029
Stop. You're being rude, Youseong.

569
00:33:09,112 --> 00:33:10,572
Nothing's going on with you two?

570
00:33:10,655 --> 00:33:11,781
Oh.

571
00:33:12,490 --> 00:33:14,826
I'm her professor, and she's my student.

572
00:33:15,702 --> 00:33:19,497
Or we might be a hat and a monkey.

573
00:33:20,665 --> 00:33:22,709
-Pardon?
-No, it's nothing.

574
00:33:25,879 --> 00:33:27,005
Hold on a second.

575
00:33:29,758 --> 00:33:31,635
Have you seen these rings before?

576
00:33:34,012 --> 00:33:35,013
[Lee Jihoon] Hmm...

577
00:33:36,431 --> 00:33:37,641
No, I've never seen them.

578
00:33:40,393 --> 00:33:41,603
Okay. Well...

579
00:33:45,607 --> 00:33:46,608
[mouthing] That's twice.

580
00:33:54,324 --> 00:33:56,910
It was wrong of me to bring Jihye up.

581
00:33:56,993 --> 00:33:57,994
I apologize.

582
00:34:00,789 --> 00:34:04,084
[sighs] But you came all the way
to my school and humiliated me.

583
00:34:04,167 --> 00:34:05,877
Haven't you gotten back at me enough?

584
00:34:05,961 --> 00:34:08,755
Hey, how is that humiliating?

585
00:34:08,838 --> 00:34:10,924
I just went there as your brother
to say hello

586
00:34:11,007 --> 00:34:13,134
and ask them
to look out for you, you brat.

587
00:34:19,599 --> 00:34:20,892
I won't tell Mom.

588
00:34:21,643 --> 00:34:23,019
She'd kill you.

589
00:34:23,103 --> 00:34:24,104
[in English] Thank you.

590
00:34:25,272 --> 00:34:26,523
So we're good now?

591
00:34:27,190 --> 00:34:29,734
[in Korean] From now on,
you show me some respect, okay?

592
00:34:31,569 --> 00:34:32,779
We'll see.

593
00:34:33,780 --> 00:34:34,781
Now go.

594
00:34:38,535 --> 00:34:39,953
[car engine starts]

595
00:34:52,507 --> 00:34:54,509
[♪ pensive music playing]

596
00:35:50,565 --> 00:35:51,566
Yeah.

597
00:35:51,858 --> 00:35:52,942
Good. Great job.

598
00:35:53,902 --> 00:35:57,739
Once you organize the data
a little better, it should pass review.

599
00:35:58,740 --> 00:36:03,536
We need to emphasize the study's
contributions beyond existing research.

600
00:36:03,620 --> 00:36:07,290
If you can articulate that well,
I think we'll be fine.

601
00:36:07,791 --> 00:36:08,792
Yes, understood.

602
00:36:10,168 --> 00:36:11,378
And what are your plans?

603
00:36:13,338 --> 00:36:15,131
You're getting your PhD this year.

604
00:36:15,215 --> 00:36:17,425
-Have you thought about doing a postdoc?
-Ah.

605
00:36:18,176 --> 00:36:19,177
Yes.

606
00:36:20,845 --> 00:36:23,056
You did both your master's
and PhD here in Korea.

607
00:36:23,890 --> 00:36:27,102
You should go abroad for your postdoc.

608
00:36:27,185 --> 00:36:31,398
Yes, actually, I've been looking
into programs in the US and Australia.

609
00:36:32,190 --> 00:36:34,693
I hear there's an opening at Stanford.

610
00:36:37,362 --> 00:36:41,783
Mm. I put in a good word for you, so feel
free to reach out if you're interested.

611
00:36:42,742 --> 00:36:44,744
Sure. Thank you.

612
00:36:45,245 --> 00:36:47,497
If it works out, you owe me dinner, okay?

613
00:36:47,580 --> 00:36:49,207
Of course.

614
00:36:50,458 --> 00:36:51,459
[knock at door]

615
00:36:51,543 --> 00:36:52,669
-Yes?
-Yes?

616
00:36:54,337 --> 00:36:56,673
-It's you.
-Hi, Sejin. Come on in.

617
00:36:57,257 --> 00:36:58,341
Here, have a seat.

618
00:37:00,301 --> 00:37:03,596
I heard things are a mess
in Professor Hwang's lab at KAIST.

619
00:37:04,597 --> 00:37:06,850
They've had three researchers leave,

620
00:37:06,933 --> 00:37:09,644
and now all their project bids
are getting pushed back.

621
00:37:10,437 --> 00:37:13,106
They might not even
be able to participate in the WRS.

622
00:37:13,189 --> 00:37:14,190
Is that true?

623
00:37:15,775 --> 00:37:16,818
Yeah, I guess.

624
00:37:16,901 --> 00:37:18,737
Wait, Professor Hwang's lab?

625
00:37:18,820 --> 00:37:20,822
-Was there an accident?
-Yeah, apparently.

626
00:37:21,614 --> 00:37:22,615
What accident?

627
00:37:23,241 --> 00:37:26,745
Well, it's not a lab accident.

628
00:37:26,828 --> 00:37:27,829
Yeah.

629
00:37:27,912 --> 00:37:28,913
[sighs]

630
00:37:30,498 --> 00:37:32,459
There was drama. Relationship drama.

631
00:37:32,542 --> 00:37:33,877
Relationship drama?

632
00:37:33,960 --> 00:37:36,379
There was this couple in the lab,

633
00:37:37,005 --> 00:37:38,423
and one of them was two-timing.

634
00:37:39,048 --> 00:37:40,425
Oh!

635
00:37:40,508 --> 00:37:43,219
So all three people
in the love triangle quit,

636
00:37:43,303 --> 00:37:46,639
and the friends they hung out with
started taking sides and fighting too.

637
00:37:47,640 --> 00:37:49,350
-It turned into a complete mess.
-Yes.

638
00:37:49,434 --> 00:37:50,435
I see.

639
00:37:50,518 --> 00:37:52,479
Well, with so many
young, single people around,

640
00:37:52,562 --> 00:37:54,773
-I guess these things happen.
-Mm.

641
00:37:55,690 --> 00:37:58,109
Maybe it's time we instituted

642
00:37:59,152 --> 00:38:02,238
a no-dating policy in our lab too?
[chuckles]

643
00:38:02,322 --> 00:38:03,656
-A no-dating policy?
-Yeah.

644
00:38:08,953 --> 00:38:12,040
You've been here a little while.
Are you settling in okay?

645
00:38:12,916 --> 00:38:15,418
When it comes to settling in, honestly...

646
00:38:16,085 --> 00:38:17,086
[Park Minjae] Hmm?

647
00:38:17,170 --> 00:38:19,255
I'd heard this was
basically a free-range lab,

648
00:38:19,339 --> 00:38:21,090
but it's even worse than I thought.

649
00:38:23,551 --> 00:38:27,931
I mean, the autonomy is nice,
but it might be a little too loose here.

650
00:38:28,014 --> 00:38:29,015
Hmm.

651
00:38:29,098 --> 00:38:33,895
Especially when romance is involved,
things can get really messy in a lab.

652
00:38:35,772 --> 00:38:37,357
[sighing] But don't worry.

653
00:38:37,440 --> 00:38:39,818
You've got me here.

654
00:38:40,735 --> 00:38:43,279
I have a hypothesis.
All I need to do is prove it.

655
00:38:43,363 --> 00:38:46,199
I'll nip this in the bud
before it causes any trouble.

656
00:38:46,282 --> 00:38:47,283
Okay.

657
00:38:47,951 --> 00:38:50,620
Even if you go to the States,
I'll hold down the fort here.

658
00:38:50,703 --> 00:38:51,704
So don't worry.

659
00:38:53,790 --> 00:38:54,999
Hey, wait.

660
00:38:56,084 --> 00:38:57,502
How did you know about that?

661
00:38:58,711 --> 00:38:59,712
What?

662
00:39:00,672 --> 00:39:02,382
I just heard about it.

663
00:39:02,465 --> 00:39:03,466
You...

664
00:39:04,092 --> 00:39:06,427
Nothing's been decided. I don't know yet.

665
00:39:07,804 --> 00:39:09,556
But the professor said it was all set.

666
00:39:09,639 --> 00:39:12,350
No way. There's still a long way to go.

667
00:39:13,560 --> 00:39:15,019
[sighs]

668
00:39:16,604 --> 00:39:19,607
-Don't tell the other guys about it, okay?
-Okay.

669
00:39:19,691 --> 00:39:20,692
[automated voice] Fifth floor.

670
00:39:25,071 --> 00:39:26,072
Going down.

671
00:39:27,574 --> 00:39:28,575
-Don't.
-Okay.

672
00:39:54,893 --> 00:39:56,895
[♪ pleasant music playing]

673
00:39:56,978 --> 00:39:57,979
[keyboard clacking]

674
00:40:15,288 --> 00:40:16,497
[sighs]

675
00:40:20,585 --> 00:40:22,253
-[Park Minjae] Lim Youjin.
-Yes?

676
00:40:22,337 --> 00:40:24,422
How's the modeling illustration
coming along?

677
00:40:25,673 --> 00:40:27,592
Oh, I'm working on it now.

678
00:40:27,675 --> 00:40:29,135
Can you finish it by today?

679
00:40:29,218 --> 00:40:30,637
Today? No.

680
00:40:33,598 --> 00:40:35,516
Can you finish it by the end of this week?

681
00:40:35,600 --> 00:40:37,393
Yeah, I can finish it by then.

682
00:40:37,977 --> 00:40:40,313
Let's pick up the pace
and make up for the delay.

683
00:40:41,022 --> 00:40:42,106
Okay.

684
00:40:48,279 --> 00:40:50,531
Okay, I'm heading out for the day.

685
00:40:50,615 --> 00:40:53,076
You guys can leave whenever you're done.

686
00:40:53,159 --> 00:40:54,160
-Okay.
-Okay.

687
00:41:00,416 --> 00:41:02,043
Hey, Lim Youjin.

688
00:41:02,126 --> 00:41:03,836
Finish that before you leave.

689
00:41:11,678 --> 00:41:15,223
[♪ pleasant music continues]

690
00:41:33,866 --> 00:41:34,993
Aren't you going home?

691
00:41:35,952 --> 00:41:37,036
[scoffs]

692
00:41:37,120 --> 00:41:38,621
I'm just going to finish this up.

693
00:41:39,664 --> 00:41:41,290
[Kim Sejin] Okay. Good luck.

694
00:41:45,920 --> 00:41:46,921
[door opens]

695
00:41:48,965 --> 00:41:49,966
[door closes]

696
00:42:17,744 --> 00:42:20,872
Lim Youjin.
Why are you coming out so late?

697
00:42:20,955 --> 00:42:22,248
Do you know what time it is?

698
00:42:22,331 --> 00:42:24,417
Weren't you even hungry? Huh?

699
00:42:26,419 --> 00:42:27,420
I'm hungry.

700
00:42:28,504 --> 00:42:29,505
Me too.

701
00:42:36,054 --> 00:42:38,347
-Slow down. Take your time.
-[sighs]

702
00:42:38,431 --> 00:42:40,058
Why haven't you eaten yet?

703
00:42:41,017 --> 00:42:42,685
You haven't even fully recovered.

704
00:42:43,644 --> 00:42:45,354
Because I had some work to finish.

705
00:42:46,564 --> 00:42:48,733
It's because of Kim Sejin,
that jerk, wasn't it?

706
00:42:49,817 --> 00:42:51,319
No.

707
00:42:51,402 --> 00:42:52,612
It wasn't Kim Sejin.

708
00:42:53,529 --> 00:42:54,989
It was Park Minjae.

709
00:42:56,783 --> 00:42:57,784
Hmm.

710
00:43:02,580 --> 00:43:04,457
Want me to order something else?

711
00:43:04,540 --> 00:43:06,751
-No.
-Do you want some sushi?

712
00:43:07,794 --> 00:43:10,630
No, my stomach would burst.
Then I'd need surgery again.

713
00:43:15,301 --> 00:43:17,345
Were you surprised today?

714
00:43:18,096 --> 00:43:20,473
-Hmm?
-Because of my brother.

715
00:43:22,183 --> 00:43:23,184
No.

716
00:43:24,102 --> 00:43:28,064
He just wanted
to see the lab and say hello.

717
00:43:28,564 --> 00:43:29,774
He won't be coming back.

718
00:43:32,693 --> 00:43:36,447
Right, who's that person
who took you to the hospital?

719
00:43:36,531 --> 00:43:37,532
A professor?

720
00:43:38,116 --> 00:43:41,452
Yeah. Professor Lee Jihoon.
Professor Talking Hat.

721
00:43:41,536 --> 00:43:42,537
Oh.

722
00:43:43,746 --> 00:43:45,957
But why didn't you tell me?

723
00:43:48,793 --> 00:43:50,711
I didn't because you never asked.

724
00:43:52,547 --> 00:43:54,173
I didn't ask because I didn't know.

725
00:43:57,885 --> 00:44:00,847
Wait, are you... jealous?

726
00:44:00,930 --> 00:44:01,931
Hmm?

727
00:44:04,559 --> 00:44:05,560
You are.

728
00:44:05,643 --> 00:44:07,145
You are jealous.

729
00:44:07,812 --> 00:44:08,813
[scoffs]

730
00:44:08,896 --> 00:44:11,566
What are you talking about?
Why would I be jealous? No way.

731
00:44:13,609 --> 00:44:15,528
You know, if...

732
00:44:16,279 --> 00:44:20,032
if you go see a musical or a movie
with some other woman,

733
00:44:20,116 --> 00:44:21,701
it doesn't bother me at all.

734
00:44:26,038 --> 00:44:28,666
[sighing]

735
00:44:30,835 --> 00:44:33,045
What do you want to do after this?

736
00:44:33,713 --> 00:44:35,840
-Hmm?
-Should we go to your place?

737
00:44:37,383 --> 00:44:39,635
Uh... we can't.

738
00:44:40,219 --> 00:44:41,262
Why not?

739
00:44:41,345 --> 00:44:43,723
Kim Sejin is watching.

740
00:44:58,696 --> 00:45:01,657
[sighs heavily]

741
00:45:01,741 --> 00:45:03,492
Do you want to sit here for a bit?

742
00:45:22,094 --> 00:45:24,722
Wearing your prosthetic leg
all day must hurt a lot.

743
00:45:25,598 --> 00:45:28,517
No, I'm used to it now, so it's fine.

744
00:45:34,106 --> 00:45:36,359
I'll be good to you from now on.

745
00:45:39,946 --> 00:45:41,197
I'll be good to you.

746
00:45:45,409 --> 00:45:48,579
Are you going to meet that woman
from the blind date again?

747
00:45:52,375 --> 00:45:54,377
Are you going to meet her again?

748
00:45:59,298 --> 00:46:00,299
I'm not.

749
00:46:03,636 --> 00:46:04,637
[Lim Youjin] Hmm.

750
00:46:04,720 --> 00:46:07,932
Once I get my PhD,
I need to go to the States for my postdoc,

751
00:46:08,015 --> 00:46:10,017
so I can't really
start seeing anyone right now.

752
00:46:24,073 --> 00:46:25,491
When would you be going?

753
00:46:26,575 --> 00:46:27,576
Uh...

754
00:46:28,744 --> 00:46:30,413
I'll be getting my degree this year,

755
00:46:30,496 --> 00:46:33,332
so maybe toward the end of this year
or sometime next year?

756
00:46:34,667 --> 00:46:35,668
Hmm.

757
00:46:35,751 --> 00:46:37,169
When would you come back?

758
00:46:37,837 --> 00:46:39,505
Two years at the earliest.

759
00:46:40,131 --> 00:46:42,133
It could be several years, though.

760
00:46:46,887 --> 00:46:48,014
But...

761
00:46:49,140 --> 00:46:51,017
it's not like you're never coming back.

762
00:46:51,100 --> 00:46:52,601
I might never come back.

763
00:46:57,106 --> 00:46:58,316
I won't come back.

764
00:47:12,455 --> 00:47:14,999
I should've told you sooner. I'm sorry.

765
00:47:20,421 --> 00:47:21,422
Hmm.

766
00:47:23,299 --> 00:47:24,675
So you're turning me down?

767
00:47:27,261 --> 00:47:29,096
You're saying you can't date me.

768
00:47:30,097 --> 00:47:31,974
You're turning me down.

769
00:47:34,143 --> 00:47:35,144
I'm sorry.

770
00:47:36,771 --> 00:47:39,690
[sighs heavily]

771
00:47:40,107 --> 00:47:44,945
It's kind of stupid
to be turned down twice by the same man.

772
00:47:46,489 --> 00:47:48,199
But what can I do?

773
00:47:50,868 --> 00:47:52,370
That's for me to deal with,

774
00:47:53,412 --> 00:47:55,373
and you have your own things to deal with.

775
00:48:03,005 --> 00:48:04,006
But...

776
00:48:05,049 --> 00:48:07,551
I thought you liked me at least a little.

777
00:48:12,556 --> 00:48:14,475
Don't be so nice to me anymore.

778
00:48:14,558 --> 00:48:15,935
It gives me the wrong idea.

779
00:48:16,018 --> 00:48:18,020
[♪ melancholy song playing]

780
00:48:38,958 --> 00:48:39,959
[Lim Youseong] Is that you, Youjin?

781
00:48:40,626 --> 00:48:41,919
Yeah.

782
00:48:42,002 --> 00:48:45,172
Do you know what time it is?
You should try to get home earlier.

783
00:48:45,256 --> 00:48:46,424
Okay.

784
00:48:46,507 --> 00:48:47,508
Lim Youjin.

785
00:48:50,594 --> 00:48:54,515
You know how much Mom and Dad
love you, right?

786
00:48:56,225 --> 00:48:57,226
What?

787
00:48:58,644 --> 00:49:00,855
Don't you ever let them down.

788
00:49:04,066 --> 00:49:05,067
Okay.

789
00:49:06,527 --> 00:49:08,696
[door lock beeps]

790
00:49:33,596 --> 00:49:34,597
[sighs softly]

791
00:49:44,231 --> 00:49:45,232
[sighs heavily]

792
00:49:48,235 --> 00:49:49,236
[sighs heavily]

793
00:49:51,280 --> 00:49:52,281
[sniffles]

794
00:49:53,324 --> 00:49:54,408
[breath trembling]

795
00:50:01,290 --> 00:50:03,459
[sobbing]

796
00:50:06,420 --> 00:50:07,630
[door lock chimes]

797
00:50:14,512 --> 00:50:15,513
[door beeps]

798
00:50:19,141 --> 00:50:20,142
[sighs softly]

799
00:50:41,956 --> 00:50:42,957
[sighs softly]

800
00:51:26,417 --> 00:51:27,710
[exhales sharply]

801
00:51:31,714 --> 00:51:32,715
[music ends]

802
00:51:39,054 --> 00:51:42,725
ENGINEERING BUILDING 3

803
00:51:44,226 --> 00:51:45,227
Good morning.

804
00:51:46,228 --> 00:51:48,689
[Kim Sejin]
It's a 90-millimeter refractor telescope.

805
00:51:48,772 --> 00:51:49,773
What are you doing?

806
00:51:49,857 --> 00:51:51,984
-You can see the details on the moon.
-Minjae.

807
00:51:52,067 --> 00:51:53,319
Sejin bought a telescope.

808
00:51:53,402 --> 00:51:55,362
-Hey, you're shaking it.
-Is it working?

809
00:51:55,446 --> 00:51:57,156
Why did you suddenly buy a telescope?

810
00:51:57,906 --> 00:52:00,326
-It's just a hobby.
-Oh.

811
00:52:00,409 --> 00:52:02,870
I heard there's going to be
a solar eclipse here soon.

812
00:52:02,953 --> 00:52:03,954
A solar eclipse?

813
00:52:04,038 --> 00:52:05,289
-A solar eclipse?
-When?

814
00:52:05,372 --> 00:52:07,374
There's a partial solar eclipse in 2030.

815
00:52:07,791 --> 00:52:09,376
-[Eom Taeho] Hmm.
-In 2030?

816
00:52:10,169 --> 00:52:11,920
-That's a long way off.
-Still far off.

817
00:52:12,004 --> 00:52:15,466
Well, I thought I could practice

818
00:52:15,549 --> 00:52:18,052
taking pictures with it
between now and then.

819
00:52:18,802 --> 00:52:19,887
All right.

820
00:52:19,970 --> 00:52:23,140
I heard the Aris meteor shower
peaks early Saturday morning.

821
00:52:23,223 --> 00:52:24,391
We could watch that.

822
00:52:24,808 --> 00:52:26,268
-What? A meteor shower?
-[Eom Taeho] Oh!

823
00:52:26,352 --> 00:52:28,020
Cool. I've only seen it in movies.

824
00:52:28,103 --> 00:52:31,607
Where you wish on shooting stars, right?
I saw it on TV.

825
00:52:31,690 --> 00:52:33,442
We don't have to go to an observatory.

826
00:52:33,525 --> 00:52:35,235
We can watch it from Sejin's place.

827
00:52:35,319 --> 00:52:37,780
Yeah. That could be
your housewarming party too, right?

828
00:52:37,863 --> 00:52:40,366
Stargazing and drinks on the rooftop?

829
00:52:40,449 --> 00:52:42,785
-Damn, it'll be romantic as hell.
-[Bae Chansoo] Oh.

830
00:52:42,868 --> 00:52:45,245
For stargazing, the weather matters a lot.

831
00:52:45,329 --> 00:52:46,330
What's the forecast?

832
00:52:46,413 --> 00:52:49,041
It's supposed to be clear.
Perfect weather for stargazing.

833
00:52:49,625 --> 00:52:52,127
Well, my place is kind of small, though.

834
00:52:53,629 --> 00:52:56,965
It doesn't matter. We'll be on the rooftop
to watch the stars anyway.

835
00:52:57,049 --> 00:52:58,384
We'll grill up there too.

836
00:52:58,467 --> 00:53:00,761
Right. We need
a picnic blanket too, right?

837
00:53:01,470 --> 00:53:03,055
And a gas burner for the barbecue.

838
00:53:03,138 --> 00:53:05,766
Oh? That sounds great. I'm excited.

839
00:53:05,849 --> 00:53:07,559
[giggling]

840
00:53:11,397 --> 00:53:12,648
You're coming too, right?

841
00:53:12,731 --> 00:53:13,732
What?

842
00:53:13,816 --> 00:53:15,067
You should come too.

843
00:53:15,150 --> 00:53:18,070
No, I'm behind on 10 papers to review.

844
00:53:18,153 --> 00:53:19,613
You guys go have fun without me.

845
00:53:19,697 --> 00:53:23,659
Come on, Minjae, you've got to have
some fun once in a while.

846
00:53:23,742 --> 00:53:26,370
He's busy with his studies.
Let's hang out by ourselves.

847
00:53:26,453 --> 00:53:27,454
Maybe you're right.

848
00:53:27,538 --> 00:53:28,539
Okay, then.

849
00:53:40,175 --> 00:53:41,260
[groans softly]

850
00:53:45,597 --> 00:53:46,932
[grunts]

851
00:54:03,157 --> 00:54:05,325
[breathing heavily]

852
00:54:06,368 --> 00:54:08,746
[distant laughter]

853
00:54:08,829 --> 00:54:10,831
[♪ pleasant music playing]

854
00:54:16,462 --> 00:54:17,463
[Eom Taeho] Oh!

855
00:54:17,546 --> 00:54:19,465
I can see it! [laughs excitedly]

856
00:54:20,048 --> 00:54:21,675
I can see the moon! [gasps]

857
00:54:21,759 --> 00:54:24,386
-Wow! It's so big.
-[Choi Hangyeol] What else can you see?

858
00:54:24,470 --> 00:54:26,221
[Eom Taeho laughing]

859
00:54:26,305 --> 00:54:28,140
The moon... Let me see.

860
00:54:28,223 --> 00:54:31,226
The moon, the moon...

861
00:54:32,811 --> 00:54:33,896
is the only thing I see.

862
00:54:33,979 --> 00:54:35,189
There are too many clouds.

863
00:54:35,272 --> 00:54:36,273
Can I take a look too?

864
00:54:36,356 --> 00:54:39,234
Well, the meteor shower is supposed
to peak between 1:00 and 2:00,

865
00:54:39,318 --> 00:54:40,819
so it should clear up by then.

866
00:54:41,570 --> 00:54:42,571
Huh? Hey.

867
00:54:42,654 --> 00:54:44,072
Hey, let me take a look too.

868
00:54:45,824 --> 00:54:48,327
The meat is burning.
Guys, come over here and eat.

869
00:54:48,410 --> 00:54:49,411
[Eom Taeho] Okay.

870
00:54:49,995 --> 00:54:51,163
[Bae Chansoo] It looks a bit different.

871
00:54:51,955 --> 00:54:53,332
[Eom Taeho] Oh, oh.

872
00:54:53,415 --> 00:54:54,750
Okay.

873
00:54:54,833 --> 00:54:56,210
Let me move the plates.

874
00:54:58,629 --> 00:55:01,965
Youjin, you're even good at grilling, huh?

875
00:55:02,049 --> 00:55:04,051
-[Lim Youjin laughs]
-[Choi Hangyeol] Where's the kimchi?

876
00:55:04,134 --> 00:55:06,428
-Kimchi.
-Kimchi.

877
00:55:06,512 --> 00:55:07,513
[Eom Taeho] Thank you.

878
00:55:07,596 --> 00:55:08,722
It looks so delicious.

879
00:55:08,805 --> 00:55:10,516
Why, thank you.

880
00:55:10,599 --> 00:55:12,684
We should've grilled some kimchi too.

881
00:55:12,768 --> 00:55:13,936
[Lim Youjin] Should I grill some?

882
00:55:14,019 --> 00:55:15,395
[Eom Taeho] No, let's eat this first.

883
00:55:15,479 --> 00:55:16,605
[Lim Youjin] Okay, I'll do it after I eat.

884
00:55:16,688 --> 00:55:19,483
[♪ melancholy music playing]

885
00:55:35,666 --> 00:55:36,750
[gasps]

886
00:55:39,211 --> 00:55:40,254
Busted.

887
00:55:40,337 --> 00:55:41,672
-Busted.
-[Lim Youjin] You have to drink.

888
00:55:41,755 --> 00:55:42,923
-Drink.
-Drink.

889
00:55:43,006 --> 00:55:44,591
Why do you guys keep targeting me?

890
00:55:44,675 --> 00:55:49,263
[all chanting] Drink!

891
00:55:49,846 --> 00:55:50,931
Drink!

892
00:55:52,307 --> 00:55:54,101
-[Eom Taeho] Bottoms up.
-[Bae Chansoo] You've got to chug it.

893
00:55:54,977 --> 00:55:57,354
[all exclaiming]

894
00:55:57,437 --> 00:55:58,939
[laughing]

895
00:55:59,606 --> 00:56:01,191
-[Lim Youjin] He's good.
-Man, he's good.

896
00:56:01,275 --> 00:56:02,568
He's knocking it back.

897
00:56:06,530 --> 00:56:07,739
[Bae Chansoo] Man, he sure can drink.

898
00:56:08,240 --> 00:56:09,449
[Lim Youjin sighing]

899
00:56:09,533 --> 00:56:10,534
Wait, what?

900
00:56:10,617 --> 00:56:12,911
-[Eom Taeho] Are we out?
-No more drinks?

901
00:56:12,995 --> 00:56:14,288
I'll go get some more.

902
00:56:14,371 --> 00:56:15,998
-No, I'll go get it.
-No.

903
00:56:16,081 --> 00:56:18,709
Come on. I'm the youngest.
I'll be right back.

904
00:56:18,792 --> 00:56:21,128
Wait, but...

905
00:56:38,854 --> 00:56:40,355
[door bell tinkles]

906
00:56:40,439 --> 00:56:42,149
[thunder rumbling]

907
00:56:47,404 --> 00:56:48,864
[rain pattering]

908
00:56:48,947 --> 00:56:49,948
Huh?

909
00:56:50,032 --> 00:56:52,034
[♪ theme song playing]

910
00:57:22,105 --> 00:57:23,607
Taeho, it's raining.

911
00:57:25,108 --> 00:57:26,109
Hey.

912
00:57:26,193 --> 00:57:27,194
Hey!

913
00:57:28,153 --> 00:57:29,613
Hey, wake up, wake up.

914
00:57:29,738 --> 00:57:32,616
Wake up.

915
00:57:32,699 --> 00:57:34,284
Let's get inside.

916
00:57:34,368 --> 00:57:36,453
Is it okay for this to get wet? Come on.

917
00:57:36,536 --> 00:57:37,537
[stutters]

918
00:57:37,621 --> 00:57:40,415
Hey, make sure to bring that in.

919
00:57:40,499 --> 00:57:43,960
Right, the power.
We need to unplug it. This...

920
00:57:45,170 --> 00:57:46,254
Hey, the cord, quick.

921
00:57:47,089 --> 00:57:48,382
Chansoo.

922
00:57:48,465 --> 00:57:49,675
Let me take this in.

923
00:57:49,758 --> 00:57:52,844
[♪ theme song continues]

924
00:58:08,694 --> 00:58:10,153
[thunder rumbling]

925
00:58:19,496 --> 00:58:21,289
[thunder rumbling]

926
00:58:49,818 --> 00:58:50,986
[grunts]

927
00:58:54,448 --> 00:58:55,532
[music ends]

928
00:58:55,615 --> 00:58:57,993
What the... Come in.

929
00:59:00,829 --> 00:59:01,997
[chuckles]

930
00:59:02,080 --> 00:59:04,624
Hey, you can't just bring it here
without telling them.

931
00:59:04,708 --> 00:59:06,626
It's fine. They don't know it was me.

932
00:59:07,794 --> 00:59:09,838
It's raining,
and he doesn't have his camera.

933
00:59:09,921 --> 00:59:11,006
He'll never find out.

934
00:59:11,840 --> 00:59:13,675
Besides, I've got an alibi.

935
00:59:14,301 --> 00:59:16,261
You'll be my alibi, right?

936
00:59:16,344 --> 00:59:17,345
No.

937
00:59:19,347 --> 00:59:20,932
Solar eclipse, my foot.

938
00:59:21,016 --> 00:59:23,935
He bought it to spy on your house.

939
00:59:26,772 --> 00:59:28,231
No way.

940
00:59:29,691 --> 00:59:31,693
If he did, he's a totally crazy pervert.

941
00:59:32,402 --> 00:59:34,196
He is a totally crazy pervert.

942
00:59:36,281 --> 00:59:37,657
No, he isn't.

943
00:59:41,203 --> 00:59:44,289
You don't have to worry
about anything anymore.

944
00:59:45,957 --> 00:59:47,042
What do you mean?

945
00:59:47,667 --> 00:59:50,212
I can wait
until you get back from the States.

946
00:59:52,005 --> 00:59:54,174
I'll be really good to you.

947
00:59:55,217 --> 00:59:56,301
[sighs softly]

948
00:59:58,804 --> 01:00:00,055
Third time's the charm,

949
01:00:01,223 --> 01:00:02,933
so I'm giving you one more chance.

950
01:00:03,850 --> 01:00:05,435
One last chance.

951
01:00:12,651 --> 01:00:14,653
Am I really that undesirable?

952
01:00:16,863 --> 01:00:18,281
[sighs]

953
01:00:20,659 --> 01:00:21,743
[stutters]

954
01:00:25,997 --> 01:00:29,501
People long ago believed
that a solar eclipse

955
01:00:30,544 --> 01:00:33,964
was the heavenly dog in the sky
swallowing the sun.

956
01:00:35,841 --> 01:00:38,009
Then the sun would be too hot for it,

957
01:00:38,093 --> 01:00:40,303
so it would spit it back out.

958
01:00:45,183 --> 01:00:46,726
That's what you're like to me.

959
01:00:48,311 --> 01:00:49,437
You're like the sun.

960
01:00:51,189 --> 01:00:52,190
Too hot.

961
01:00:58,738 --> 01:00:59,739
Then...

962
01:01:02,576 --> 01:01:03,827
Try swallowing it anyway.

963
01:01:05,370 --> 01:01:08,373
If it's too hot, you can spit it back out.

964
01:01:10,083 --> 01:01:12,836
Imagine how painful it must be
to swallow the sun,

965
01:01:13,628 --> 01:01:15,380
only to have to spit it back out.

966
01:01:16,965 --> 01:01:19,259
I can't do that.

967
01:01:19,759 --> 01:01:21,303
I don't think I can.

968
01:01:25,682 --> 01:01:27,017
I don't want that anymore.

969
01:01:27,100 --> 01:01:29,728
I just want something
easy and comfortable.

970
01:01:32,439 --> 01:01:35,191
That's the kind of guy I am.

971
01:01:39,946 --> 01:01:41,031
You're an idiot.

972
01:01:41,615 --> 01:01:42,741
You're such a coward.

973
01:01:44,701 --> 01:01:46,536
Stay that way for the rest of your life.

974
01:01:58,089 --> 01:01:59,883
[door lock beeps]

975
01:02:02,510 --> 01:02:04,512
[♪ emotional song playing]

976
01:02:21,529 --> 01:02:23,949
[rain pattering]

977
01:02:26,326 --> 01:02:27,494
What an idiot.

978
01:02:28,370 --> 01:02:30,246
Stay that way for the rest of your life.
[sobbing]

979
01:02:59,567 --> 01:03:00,735
Let's get inside.

980
01:03:01,361 --> 01:03:02,570
You'll catch a cold.

981
01:03:33,977 --> 01:03:35,395
[Lim Youjin sobbing]

982
01:03:38,398 --> 01:03:39,399
Let go.

983
01:03:39,983 --> 01:03:41,317
Let go!

984
01:03:41,526 --> 01:03:42,610
[grunts]

985
01:03:43,028 --> 01:03:45,280
[crying]

986
01:04:05,675 --> 01:04:06,676
Once...

987
01:04:07,927 --> 01:04:10,013
I swallow something, I never spit it out.

988
01:04:13,433 --> 01:04:16,102
I'd never spit it out,
even if it burned me alive.

989
01:04:20,607 --> 01:04:21,983
There's no going back.

990
01:04:23,985 --> 01:04:25,653
I have to see it through to the end.

991
01:04:30,283 --> 01:04:31,451
Do you still want this?

992
01:04:39,000 --> 01:04:43,671
[rain intensifies]

993
01:05:07,654 --> 01:05:11,574
BETWEEN STEPS

994
01:05:47,694 --> 01:05:49,404
[Park Minjae] How about
we don't tell anyone

995
01:05:49,487 --> 01:05:51,072
that we're dating for now?

996
01:05:51,156 --> 01:05:52,407
He's asleep.

997
01:05:52,490 --> 01:05:54,659
[Lim Youjin] Kim Sejin.
He's such a schemer. Okay?

998
01:05:54,742 --> 01:05:56,202
He's a crazy little suck-up.

999
01:05:56,286 --> 01:05:58,371
But why do I even have
to compete with him?

1000
01:05:58,454 --> 01:06:00,081
Park Minjae is mine.

1001
01:06:00,165 --> 01:06:01,249
We used to date.

1002
01:06:01,332 --> 01:06:02,417
You two used to date?

1003
01:06:02,500 --> 01:06:03,585
[Cha Seohyun] I'm sleeping over.

1004
01:06:03,668 --> 01:06:05,879
Me too. I can stay the night here too.

1005
01:06:05,962 --> 01:06:07,630
Like I said, she's my best friend.

1006
01:06:07,714 --> 01:06:10,925
You can't meet up with her alone
or have her over at your place.

1007
01:06:11,009 --> 01:06:12,802
[Lim Youjin] Park Minjae is mine.

1008
01:06:12,886 --> 01:06:14,512
No one's taking you away from me.
